Medusa Constable QEMU smoke test
================================

This test boots an x86-64 Medusa kernel with the Constable reference
authorization server in a minimal initramfs.  It verifies all of the
behavior-preserving migration boundary:

  * Linux reaches /sbin/init with Medusa enabled.
  * The kernel starts Constable before init.
  * Constable connects to /dev/medusa using protocol version 3.
  * The first mkdir decision is delegated to Constable.
  * Constable updates the parent directory's med_oact cache bitmap.
  * A second mkdir on the same parent does not produce another delegated
    decision.

The kernel must be configured with:

  CONFIG_SECURITY_MEDUSA=y
  CONFIG_SECURITY_MEDUSA_START_AUTH_SERVER_BEFORE_INIT=y
  CONFIG_SECURITY_MEDUSA_AUTH_SERVER_TRIGGER="/sbin/init"
  CONFIG_SECURITY_MEDUSA_AUTH_SERVER_LOADER="/sbin/init-constable.sh"

Build Constable and BusyBox as static x86-64 executables, then run:

  tools/testing/selftests/medusa/qemu/run.sh \
    path/to/arch/x86/boot/bzImage \
    path/to/constable \
    path/to/busybox

The test exits successfully only after observing:

  MEDUSA_QEMU_PASS: delegated=1 cached=1

QEMU_ACCEL, QEMU_CPU, and QEMU_TIMEOUT may be overridden in the environment.
